+# Hegel property-based testing report — `rasn`
+
+Property-based tests added with [hegel](https://hegel.dev) (`hegeltest`) targeting
+the BER / CER / DER / OER / COER codecs of the `rasn` ASN.1 framework. All new
+tests live in `tests/fuzz.rs`, in a `mod hegel_props` block appended after the
+existing corpus-replay fuzz tests (whose bug classes they generalize).
+
+Dev-dependencies added to `rasn`: `hegeltest`, `num-bigint` (bignum INTEGER
+generation), `chrono` (typed time values).
+
+## 1. Properties added
+
+13 live properties plus 2 pinned bug reproducers. One property per test.
+
+**Roundtrip (encode → decode == identity):**
+- `open_roundtrip_ber` / `open_roundtrip_der` / `open_roundtrip_cer` — the crown
+  roundtrip over generated `Open` (CHOICE) values covering BIT STRING, BOOLEAN,
+  GeneralizedTime, INTEGER (incl. bignum/negative/boundary), NULL, OID,
+  OCTET STRING, UniversalString, UTCTime, VisibleString, and nested InstanceOf.
+- `model_roundtrip_all_codecs` — a derived `SEQUENCE` with `Option`,
+  `SEQUENCE OF`, and `ENUMERATED` fields, roundtripped through ber/der/cer/oer/coer.
+- `choice_roundtrip_ber_der` — a derived CHOICE with a nested SEQUENCE arm.
+- `integer_roundtrip` — INTEGER over ber/der/cer/oer.
+- `octet_string_roundtrip`, `safe_oid_roundtrip` — primitives incl. empty inputs.
+
+**Cross-codec / canonicity:**
+- `der_encoding_decodes_under_ber` — DER (a subset of BER) decodes under BER to
+  the same value.
+- `der_is_canonical_fixpoint` — re-encoding a DER-decoded value reproduces the
+  exact bytes (fixpoint). Oracle-independent.
+- `integer_der_fixpoint` — same fixpoint check specialized to INTEGER (catches
+  non-minimal integer encodings).
+
+**Untrusted-input robustness (highest value):**
+- `arbitrary_bytes_never_panic` — arbitrary byte strings (≤256 B) decoded as
+  Open/bool/Integer/OctetString/OID/BitString/Model/Payload across ber/der/cer/oer
+  must return Ok or Err, never panic/OOM/hang.
+- `corrupted_encoding_never_panics` — encode a valid value, flip a byte or
+  truncate, decode: Ok or Err, never panic.
+- `huge_declared_length_is_rejected` — a long-form length declaring ≥2^16 bytes
+  of content with only 2 content bytes present must be rejected (no gigabyte
+  pre-allocation).
+- `nested_length_bomb_is_graceful` — indefinite-length SEQUENCE nested up to 4000
+  deep must be rejected gracefully, not stack-overflow.
+
+## 2. Bugs found (pinned, deterministically failing)
+
+Two real, oracle-independent bugs in the OID encoder, both reachable from the
+crate's own public API (`ObjectIdentifier::new` accepts the inputs). Both are
+pinned as deterministic KNOWN-FAILURE tests, per instructions — **not fixed**.
+
+**BUG 1 — silent OID value corruption (`bug_oid_low_first_arc_roundtrip_corruption`).**
+`ObjectIdentifier::new` validates only `first_arc <= 2` (`is_valid_oid` in
+`src/types/oid.rs:7`). X.660 additionally requires the second arc to be `< 40`
+when the first arc is 0 or 1. The BER encoder packs `first*40 + second` into a
+single subidentifier (`src/ber/enc.rs:36`), and the decoder unpacks it as
+`first = min(value/40, 2)`. So an accepted OID like `0.40` round-trips to `1.0`,
+and `0.999` to `2.919` — silent corruption of a decoded value. Minimal
+counterexample: `0.40 → 1.0`.
+
+**BUG 2 — INTEGER/OID arithmetic overflow (`bug_oid_second_arc_overflow`).**
+The same `first * (MAX_OID_SECOND_OCTET + 1) + second` at `src/ber/enc.rs:36` is
+computed in `u32` with no overflow guard. `ObjectIdentifier::new` accepts
+`first == 2` with an arbitrary `u32` second arc, so `2.(u32::MAX-79 .. u32::MAX)`
+overflows: **panic** (`attempt to add with overflow`) in a debug build, silent
+**wraparound → corrupt encoding** in a release build. The pinned test asserts the
+roundtrip so it fails under both profiles. Minimal counterexample:
+`2.4294967216`.
+
+Both are validation gaps: `is_valid_oid` is too permissive relative to what the
+encoder can faithfully represent.
+
+## 3. Process-aborting bugs
+
+None found. The depth guard (`DecodeErrorKind::ExceedsMaxParseDepth`, unit-tested
+in `tests/recursiveDepth.rs`) correctly rejects deep nesting — `nested_length_bomb_is_graceful`
+confirmed graceful rejection up to depth 4000 with no stack overflow. Crafted huge
+length prefixes are rejected with `Incomplete` and no gigabyte allocation. No
+`#[ignore]`d reproducers were needed.
+
+## 4. Validation performed
+
+- **Liveness / mutation:** inverting the `der_is_canonical_fixpoint` assertion
+  produced a shrunk counterexample (`[5, 0]`), confirming the test is live; reverted.
+- **High-count exploratory run:** all 13 live properties were run at 2000 cases
+  (robustness sweep at its committed 400) with no new failures.
+- **Determinism of pins:** both bug tests reproduce on every run with a boosted
+  generator that always lands in the buggy region, and print stable minimal
+  counterexamples.
+
+## 5. How to run / maintenance notes
+
+```
+cargo test -p rasn --test fuzz hegel_props            # all new properties
+cargo test -p rasn --test fuzz hegel_props -- --skip bug_   # green subset only
+```
+
+Expected result: **40 pass, 2 fail** (the two pinned OID bugs). The two failures
+are intentional bug documentation and should stay red until the OID validation /
+encoding is fixed. `.hegel/` (the failure-replay DB) is git-ignored.
+
+Generators deliberately restrict OIDs to the well-formed subset in
+`arb_safe_oid` so the roundtrip/fixpoint/robustness properties stay green; the
+excluded (buggy) OID region is covered exclusively by the two pinned tests.
+UTCTime generation is bounded to years 1970–2049 (the 2-digit-year domain) and
+whole seconds, matching the type's documented representation.
